.env*

# The one exception, and it has to sit after the .env patterns above to win.
# .env.example carries no values — only the two variable names the build
# reads, VITE_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION and VITE_BING_SITE_VERIFICATION, with
# empty right-hand sides and a note on where each token comes from. Without
# it, the fact that those variables exist at all lives only in vite.config.js,
# and a fresh clone deploys with no way to verify the domain.
!.env.example

# Superpowers brainstorming visual companion
.superpowers/

# Downloaded Claude skills collection — not part of the site source.
# Ignored so oxlint stops scanning its reference .jsx/.js files, which
# produced warnings unrelated to anything in src/.
Claude Skills/
.claude/

# Same reason, later arrivals: vendored agent skills, and the local MCP server
# list. None of it is site source, all of it is reproducible from its own
# installer, and .agents/ alone is 2.2 MB that oxlint was scanning and
# reporting warnings out of.
.agents/
.impeccable/
skills-lock.json
.mcp.json

# Generated at build time from the data modules — see scripts/knowledge.mjs
public/knowledge.json

# Same, from scripts/generate-static.mjs. These carry the site's own URL and,
# in llms.txt, its prices. They were hand-maintained and llms.txt drifted two
# price revisions behind the tiers it quoted — while telling the reader it did
# not repeat any figure that came from a data file. Tracking a generated file
# is what makes that possible, so they are not tracked.
public/sitemap.xml
public/robots.txt
public/llms.txt
